<article class="env-lemma" id="08ZZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08ZZ">Lemma <span data-tag="08ZZ">5.22.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a profinite space. Every open covering of $X$ has a refinement by a finite covering $X = \coprod U_ i$ with $U_ i$ open and closed. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X_ i$ as a limit of an inverse system of finite discrete spaces over a directed set $I$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/08ZY" data-tag="08ZY">5.22.2</a>). Denote $f_ i : X \to X_ i$ the projection. For every point $x = (x_ i) \in X$ a fundamental system of open neighbourhoods is the collection $f_ i^{-1}(\{ x_ i\} )$. Thus, as $X$ is quasi-compact, we may assume we have an open covering 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X = f_{i_1}^{-1}(\{ x_{i_1}\} ) \cup \ldots \cup f_{i_ n}^{-1}(\{ x_{i_ n}\} )  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Choose $i \in I$ with $i \geq i_ j$ for $j = 1, \ldots , n$ (this is possible as $I$ is a directed set). Then we see that the covering 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X = \coprod \nolimits _{t \in X_ i} f_ i^{-1}(\{ t\} )  \]
</div>
    <p>
       refines the given covering and is of the desired form. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>